1
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:09,850
Your browser first asks DNS where example.com actually lives.

2
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:12,665
Then it opens an encrypted TLS

3
00:00:12,665 --> 00:00:15,850
connection to the nearest edge server.

4
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:20,054
A load balancer forwards the request

5
00:00:20,054 --> 00:00:23,850
to whichever app server is healthy.

6
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:29,850
The app server reads what it needs from the database.

7
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,916
Finally, the response travels all

8
00:00:32,916 --> 00:00:35,850
the way back and your page renders.
